    {
      "id": "n5-u03-g02",
      "title": "〜時〜分 — telling the time",
      "pattern": "〜時〜分です / 今何時ですか",
      "meaning": "It's ~ o'clock and ~ minutes / What time is it now?",
      "explanation": "For hours, say the number plus 時 (じ): 三時 is three o'clock. For minutes, say the number plus 分, which is read ふん or ぷん depending on the number: 五分 (ごふん), 十分 (じゅっぷん). 半 means \"half past\": 二時半 is 2:30. To ask the time, say 今何時ですか — \"What time is it now?\" 午前 (a.m.) and 午後 (p.m.) go before the time: 午後三時 is 3 p.m.",
      "notes": [
        "Special hour readings: 四時 (よじ), 七時 (しちじ), 九時 (くじ).",
        "Special minute readings: 一分 (いっぷん), 三分 (さんぷん), 四分 (よんぷん), 六分 (ろっぷん), 八分 (はっぷん), 十分 (じゅっぷん).",
        "11 and 12 are simply 十一 (じゅういち) and 十二 (じゅうに): 十二時 is twelve o'clock."
      ],
