    {
      "id": "n5-u03-g03",
      "title": "〜から〜まで — from ~ until ~",
      "pattern": "A から B まで",
      "meaning": "from A until B",
      "explanation": "から marks a starting point and まで marks an end point. They come after the word they belong to, so 九時から means \"from nine\" and 五時まで means \"until five\". With です you can give opening hours or schedules: 銀行は九時から三時までです — The bank is open from nine to three. You can also use just one of them: 授業は九時からです — Class is from nine (starts at nine).",
      "notes": [
        "から and まで also work with days: 月曜日から金曜日まで (Monday to Friday).",
        "They work with places too (駅から学校まで — from the station to school); you'll use that with verbs in Unit 4."
